{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RowStandardTableau","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytMathlibBridge","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SytRowSuperstandard","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.LengthAdditive"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.length_dOf_smul_eq_add_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.length_dOf_smul_eq_add_iff","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L161-L177","doc":"**The length half of Mathas 3.13, as a combinatorial criterion.**\n\nFor a tableau factorisation `t = w • g`, the length is additive —\n`ℓ(d(t)) = ℓ(w) + ℓ(d(g))` — **exactly when `w` undoes none of `d(g)`'s\ninversions**.\n\nThe right-hand side is decidable and mentions no lengths and no reduced words,\nwhich is what makes it checkable for a proposed Garnir tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.toFinSucc_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.toFinSucc_mul","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L153-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.toFinSucc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.toFinSucc","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L148-L151","doc":"The cast `Perm (Fin (nOf μ)) ≃ Perm (Fin (n+1))` induced by `nOf μ = n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.refTab_symm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.refTab_symm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L127-L139","doc":"**The reference tableau in closed form.**  The label in cell `(i, j)` of `t^μ`\nis `rowPrefix μ i + j` — the number of cells in the rows above, plus the offset\nalong the row.  (`rowPrefix μ i = ∑_{i' < i} μ.rowLen i'`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.equivPerm_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.equivPerm_apply","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.equivPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.equivPerm","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L110-L117","doc":"**The action is simply transitive**: `dOf` is a bijection from `μ`-tableaux to\npermutations.\n\nThis is the non-vacuity statement for everything above — `dOf` is not merely\n*some* map to permutations, it identifies the two sets, so a claim about `d(t)`\nis a claim about every permutation and vice versa. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L107-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_smul_refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_smul_refTab","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L102-L105","doc":"`dOf` recovers the acting permutation: `d(σ • t^μ) = σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_injective","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L97-L100","doc":"`dOf` is injective: a tableau is determined by its permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_smul","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L87-L95","doc":"**The factorisation bridge.**  A tableau factorisation `t = w • g` becomes the\npermutation factorisation `d(t) = w * d(g)`.\n\nThis is what lets a statement about tableaux be handed to\n`QOU.Hecke.Inversions.length_mul_eq_add_iff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_refTab","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L83-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_unique","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L73-L81","doc":"**Uniqueness**: nothing else carries the reference tableau to `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.smul_refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.smul_refTab","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L65-L71","doc":"**The defining property**: `d(t)` carries the reference tableau to `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf_apply","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L62-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.dOf","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L55-L60","doc":"**`d(t)`** — the permutation carrying the reference tableau to `t`.\n\nAs an `Equiv` this is `t^μ` followed by `t⁻¹`; `smul_refTab` below is the\ncharacterising property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TableauPerm.refTab","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TableauPerm.lean#L50-L53","doc":"The **row-superstandard tableau** `t^μ`, used as the origin of the `S_n`-action\non `μ`-tableaux. ","signatureChunk":0}]}